        "original_id": "ac3794c0-1f92-5f24-8741-2302f2e6d3f8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Friso, Alexander the Great\n- Places: Punjab, Frisia\n- Concepts: Frisian origin legends, medieval manuscripts\n\nFacts:\n- A manuscript written in a language spoken between the 8th and 16th centuries states that Friso was a leader of Frisian colonists.\n- The manuscript says the Frisian colonists had been settled in the Punjab for well over a millennium before Alexander the Great discovered them.\n- The account presents Friso as part of a Frisian origin legend preserved in a medieval manuscript tradition.",
