      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "fead6c55-96a7-5553-89fe-5b5c4e61d411",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Oera Linda Book\n- Languages: Old Frisian\n- People: Friso, Martinus Hamconius, Alexander the Great\n- Places: Frisia, Punjab, Rhine, Weser, European North Sea coast\n- Topics: Frisian colonists, historical mythology, religious themes\n\nFacts:\n- The Oera Linda Book is a manuscript written in a form of Old Frisian that purports to cover historical, mythological, and religious themes from 2194 BCE to 803 CE.\n- Old Frisian is a West Germanic language spoken between the 8th and 16th centuries in the area between the Rhine and Weser on the European North Sea coast.\n- In the 17th century, Martinus Hamconius wrote the chronicle \"Frisia seu de viris rebusque illustribus,\" which said that Friso was a leader of Frisian colonists settled in the Punjab for well over a millennium when Alexander the Great discovered them.\n- In the 19th century, the Oera Linda Book also described Friso as a leader of Frisian colonists who had been settled in the Punjab for well over a millennium when they were discovered by Alexander the Great.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
